<x:xmpmeta xmlns:x="adobe:ns:meta/">
  <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#">
    <rdf:Description xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" rdf:about="">
      <dc:title>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">like finding a path in the water, behind the wave</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;
  &lt;i&gt;Some days are happier than others.&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
  &lt;i&gt;On the good days, it isnâ€™t hard at all for Catra to look at Adora, steal kisses down her neck right as she puts up her hair. It isnâ€™t hard for her to jump into She-Raâ€™s arms no matter who is around and let her play with her hair, fingers petting her on the head, pressing into her heart. On the bad days, Catra frightens herself so much that she wakes up after barely even going to sleep with soundless cries stuck to the nose, at her temple, explosives in her eyes. And, every time, Adora wakes too.&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;-&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;In which Catra finds out how much Adora truly loves her. Or, a crisis held together only by Adora's inability to let Catra go.&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
      <dc:creator>
